Story: As a Scrum Master, I want to see average cycle time broken down by pipeline stage for each sprint so that I can identify where stories are getting stuck.

Acceptance criteria:
- A visible 'Cycle Time by Stage' card appears in index.html with a table whose column headers are exactly: Sprint, Pull, Story, Code, Test, Code Review, AC Check, Deploy.
- Each cell value is the arithmetic mean of stage_times[stage] across all items in that sprint that have a numeric (non-null, non-undefined) value for that stage, displayed as a number rounded to one decimal place followed by 's' (e.g., '14.3s').
- When no items in a sprint have a numeric value for a given stage, the cell displays exactly '—'.
- Rows are sorted descending by sprint_number and at most 5 rows are displayed, consistent with the sprint window used in the Sprint Health Summary card.
- Feature is implemented directly within index.html — no changes to any other file.

Data store fields: ac_check_reason, ac_check_verdict, acceptance_criteria, code_review_reason, code_review_verdict, deployed, diff, hermes_reason, hermes_verdict, id, idea, in_sprint, retro_context, source, sprint_number, sprint_wisdom, stage_times, started, status, story, summary, test_results, tokens_in, tokens_out
Status values: done | failed
Pipeline: pull → story → code → test → code_review → ac_check → deploy → done
Field types: acceptance_criteria: Array<string>; stage_times: object<{ac_check, code, code_review, deploy, done, pull, story, test}>; test_results: Array<{message: string, status: "pass"}>

